<!--
    angr ReturnDuplicatorHigh, per-edge const narrowing (option earlyreturn,
    default-OFF; ELEM 4111), S8 goto-quality sub-stage.

    ActionEarlyReturn peels ONLY the constant arm of a MIXED return phi
    (v = MULTIEQUAL(#K, var); return v) into its own per-predecessor return K,
    leaving the variable body return merged. The whole-block returndup gate
    (returndup_is_const_ret) requires the ENTIRE return value const, so it rejects
    this mixed diamond outright; earlyreturn reaches it via a per-edge const check
    and reuses the same node_split machinery. branchflip + ifelseflatten (both
    default-on) then orient the peeled guard as the if-true and de-indent the body.

    Witness (self-contained, no relocations): coreutils factor sub_eb2e @ 0xeb2e, a
    real isdigit-style character-class check compiled at -O0, whose two arms assign
    constants merged at a single return of the register phi (rax = MULTIEQUAL of the
    two arm values). 72 bytes verbatim from the O0/coreutils/factor corpus binary.

    Pass 1 (option earlyreturn off): kuna keeps the merged diamond - a single
    trailing return reached from both arms (if (guard) { v = 0 } else { v = 1 }
    return v;), so the token return appears exactly ONCE.
    Pass 2 (option earlyreturn on): the constant guard arm is peeled to its own
    early return, so there are TWO returns (if (!guard) { return 1; } return 0;) and
    the earlyreturn: hoisted line is logged. return appears TWICE. Total 3.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000">
f30f1efa554889e5897dfc8b45fc83e83083f8360f97c284d2752648baff037e0000007e0089c148d3ea4889d083e0014885c00f95c084c07407b801000000eb05b8000000005dc3
</bytechunk>
